			<div class="content" id="post-content-2362652">
									

<p>I really don't know what to think of this. It didn't have much of an effect on me. Perhaps I'm too attached to my own recent creation story.</p>
<p>I'm not fond of Pangloss as a character or concept (especially because I use Wondertainment to fill that role), and this tale didn't do much to establish Pangloss as an actual, meaningful identity that can stand on its own.</p>
<p>Deer I can speak more clearly on, and I can be a bit more specific. Deer actually has hidden historical precedent and origin, though admittedly one that neither Dmatix or I have ever actually explored. He's the ever-reincarnating <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sabbatai_Zevi">Sabbatai Zevi</a> (Sabbatai is literally &quot;Saturn&quot;. Zevi isn't directly &quot;Deer&quot;, I don't think, but its close enough to be a pun. Ask Dmatix, he knows)</p>
<p>While there's always room for re-interpretation, even without the historical context SD doesn't feel like a proper fit for a creation myth. He's a shuckster, a huckster, the buzzard who will pick up the scraps of the greater powers and sell them back to you at 3000% markup. At the very greatest, I could see him as a sort of trickster demigod, but not a major mover and shaker - why act when others can act instead and you can profit off of them? Making him mad takes away a lot of his character and agency - Deer's a dick mostly because he just feels like it.</p>
<p>So yeah. Holding off on voting. Leaning towards downvote for lack of engagement.</p>

							</div>

								
					
