<p>Sorry it didn't do much for you.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Perhaps I'm too attached to my own recent creation story.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I actually almost didn't post this because I didn't want to clash with the cool Djoricverse thing you have going, buuuuut I felt that they were dissimilar enough and patience is not one of my virtues.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I'm not fond of Pangloss as a character or concept (especially because I use Wondertainment to fill that role), and this tale didn't do much to establish Pangloss as an actual, meaningful identity that can stand on its own.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I knew that you weren't particularly fond of Pangloss, hadn't realized it was because of Wondertainment. Oh well, maybe this will be the first step to giving Pangloss some substance as a meaningful character.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Deer actually has hidden historical precedent and origin</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Ah. Crud. Had not realized that there was historical significance.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>He's a shuckster, a huckster, the buzzard who will pick up the scraps of the greater powers and sell them back to you at 3000% markup.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>At the very greatest, I could see him as a sort of trickster demigod, but not a major mover and shaker - why act when others can act instead and you can profit off of them?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would like to disagree with the first part of this and build off of the second. I actually have a hard time picturing him as only a demigod. We've already seen him hand several gods' backsides to them on silver platters and has managed to gain from it. We've also seen him toy around with mere mortals. The best way that I could reconcile this was to have him be someone who still bothers with puny humans because he is, on some level, human, and be more powerful than most deities so he can do the aforementioned posterior serving. Also, he is kind of profiting off of someone else's work here; just look at all these newly created people sitting around, just waiting to be ruled!</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Making him mad takes away a lot of his character and agency - Deer's a dick mostly because he just feels like it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I see no reason why he can't be both.</p>
