<p><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/pangloss#pages">Only one other tale besides this</a>. Where's this other tale you're getting?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Furthermore, the reason he exists is to make fun of artsy types.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>The best way to deal with the character, in my head, is to destroy him in order to highlight the pointlessness of his poetic attitude towards everything.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I already had my fill of that in a 23-part epic around a certain GoI. If Pangloss does exist to make fun of artsy types (which I wanna see Flameshirt's word on; though I can buy it anyway), I guess I can't see how continuing to kill him off highlights the pointlessness? There's ways to drive people to despair without resulting in death. Not that any of it would fit this tale anyway, since it's explicitly a &quot;beginning&quot;. So I guess I'm being pedantic &lt;.&lt;</p>

