<p>Now listen here Mac,</p>
<p>In this canon<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-545091-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-545091-1')">1</a></sup> Pangloss is tied with what is basically the embodiment of observation for the title of oldest thing in existence. In Christian tradition, God, the oldest thing in existence, literally the only true source of good and hope for this small blue speck we live on, was murdered in one of the most excruciating ways known to man at that time (granted, He did get better). Why, then, do you expect me <em>not</em> to torment and destroy Pangloss? if only after a good deal of buildup.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-545091-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-545091-1')">1</a>. and please not that I run multiple headcanons at once so not even everything I write about Pangloss should be tied to this.</div>
</div>

